Debugging “Disk Full” on EC2 (quick workflow)

✅ Confirm what’s full: df -h (space) vs df -i (inodes)
🔎 Find the biggest consumers: du -xh / --max-depth=2 | sort -h
🗂️ Check common hotspots:
/var/log (unrotated logs)
/tmp and /var/tmp (temp spill)
Docker storage (/var/lib/docker)
Old backups/artifacts
🧹 Cleanup safely: rotate/truncate logs, remove unused images/containers, delete stale temp files
💾 Fix permanently: resize/add EBS, split root vs data volume, centralize logs, set disk alerts at 70/80/90%
